{
  "name": "cis_controls",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "tag": "cis_site_version",
      "value": "8.1"
    },
    {
      "tag": "revision_date",
      "value": "2025-03"
    },
    {
      "tag": "pages_read_on",
      "value": "2026-10-30"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A LinkML model of the structure of the CIS Critical Security Controls (CIS Controls), Version 8.1, which the Center for Internet Security (CIS) publishes. It models the Controls and the Safeguards of each Control. For each Safeguard it records the asset class, the security function and the Implementation Groups that include it. It names each Control and Safeguard by its number and carries none of CIS's text.",
  "title": "CIS Critical Security Controls",
  "comments": [
    "The version is the label that the pages of CIS's guide carry for its revision of March 2025. CIS's site calls the edition Version 8.1. The guide's change log names two minor revisions of it, v8.1.1 in August 2024 and v8.1.2 in March 2025. They corrected small errors, among them the security function of two Safeguards. The source is CIS's page for Version 8.1. scripts/check_upstream_release.py holds the same pins and reports when CIS's pages name a newer version.",
    "CIS licenses the CIS Controls under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 and requires its prior approval for commercial use, while this schema is Apache-2.0. So the schema carries no CIS text: no Control or Safeguard title or description, and none of the guide's overviews or explanations. The descriptions here are this project's own words. The text slots, title and description, are optional and hold text their user has the right to use; NOTICE says what CIS's licence allows.",
    "The edition holds 18 Controls and 153 Safeguards. Implementation Group 1 holds 56 of the Safeguards, Implementation Group 2 adds 74 to make 130, and Implementation Group 3 adds the last 23, so it holds all 153. CIS's pages on the CIS Controls list and on each Implementation Group state these numbers."
  ],
  "source": "https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1",
  "see_also": [
    "https://lmodel.github.io/cis-controls",
    "https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/cis-controls-list",
    "https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/implementation-groups",
    "https://www.cisecurity.org/insights/white-papers/guide-to-asset-classes-cis-critical-security-controls-v8-1"
  ],
  "id": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cis-controls",
  "version": "8.1.2",
  "imports": [
    "linkml:types"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "prefixes": [
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "cis_controls",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cis-controls/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "linkml",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/linkml/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "nist_csf_v2",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-csf-v2/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "oscal",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/oscal/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "schema",
      "prefix_reference": "http://schema.org/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "xsd",
      "prefix_reference": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
    }
  ],
  "default_prefix": "cis_controls",
  "default_range": "string",
  "types": [
    {
      "name": "cis_control_identifier",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cis-controls/CisControlIdentifier",
      "description": "A Control's identifier: its number from 1 to 18, as CIS writes it, such as 4 for Control 4.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cis-controls",
      "typeof": "string",
      "base": "str",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
      "pattern": "^([1-9]|1[0-8])$",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "cis_safeguard_identifier",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cis-controls/CisSafeguardIdentifier",
      "description": "A Safeguard's identifier, as CIS writes it: the number of its Control, a dot and the Safeguard's number within the Control, such as 4.1 for Safeguard 4.1.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cis-controls",
      "typeof": "string",
      "base": "str",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
      "pattern": "^([1-9]|1[0-8])\\.[1-9][0-9]?$",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "string",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/String",
      "description": "A character string",
      "notes": [
        "In RDF serializations, a slot with range of string is treated as a literal or type xsd:string. If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"string\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Text"
      ],
      "base": "str",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
